MOBIUS LOOP  (one-sided non-orientable surface)

PARAMETRIC TYPE
  Regular surface immersion  R^2 -> R^3
  Parameters:  u  (angular / twist),  v  (width)

EQUATIONS
  x(u,v) = ( 1 + (v/2) cos(u/2) ) cos u
  y(u,v) = ( 1 + (v/2) cos(u/2) ) sin u
  z(u,v) = (v/2) sin(u/2)

VARIABLES
  u  :  [0, 2pi]     once around the loop, half-twist in argument u/2
  v  :  [-1, 1]      across the strip  (width scale set by the factor 1/2)
  R  =  1            centerline radius (the leading "1")

FUNDAMENTALS
  Topology     :  non-orientable, one boundary component
  Identification :  (u,v) ~ (u+2pi, -v)   half-twist glue
  Euler char.  :  chi = 0
  Boundary     :  one closed curve (not two, unlike a cylinder)
  Local type   :  ruled surface; centerline is a circle of radius 1
  Twist        :  180 deg per full circuit in u

NOTES
  At v = 0 the map traces the unit circle in the xy-plane.
  The cos(u/2), sin(u/2) terms implement the half-twist.
  Traversing u from 0 to 4pi returns to the same point with the
  same normal (two full trips restore orientation).
